proof.text:
For witnesses fix the finite ring $P_n$. The comparison inverse image $
u_T^*$ is exact and commutes with cohomology. More explicitly exactness preserves the kernels and cokernels in the good truncation formulas, so termwise $
u_T^*	au^{\le m}=	au^{\le m}
u_T^*$ and $
u_T^*	au^{\ge m+1}=	au^{\ge m+1}
u_T^*$, naturally; these identifications descend through quasi-isomorphisms. Applying them to $\alpha_n$ gives the claimed levelwise origins and compatibility with all strict transitions. The truncated etale objects are still bounded below: truncating a bounded-below cohomological interval retains its lower bound or replaces it by $m+1$. This proves the unconditional, levelwise part of the witness clause. In Lean the retained origin object is the actual standard truncation of the original etale object. Its alpha is constructed by mapping the truncated fixed-ring comparison through finiteCoefficientRealization, composing with mapDerivedCategoryCompIso, and taking the fully faithful preimage through the inclusion of D+. Thus no arbitrary origin witness is selected. The original normalization compatibility becomes a semilinear compatibility square by naturality of the scalar-restriction comparison and the unit law unit_mateEquiv_symm. For lower truncation, postcompose with the exact-restriction truncation comparison and use the counit universal property. For upper truncation, precompose with the comparison inverse and use the unit universal property. Naturality then reduces both squares to the untruncated semilinear square.
